    },
    {
      "id": "Bj2jhZJMI6FkshZsMJJeG",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -41983.87157933948,
      "y": -13060.89388634513,
      "width": 1374.699479844835,
      "height": 147.5,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "#121212",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 2,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aDt",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 370059368,
      "version": 843,
      "versionNonce": 722207477,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1776233590119,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "step 5: High level design",
      "fontSize": 118.00000000000004,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "step 5: High level design",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "ElxeCHGupdqEkk0KRwyEa",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -42062.510629190714,
      "y": -16319.936002938999,
      "width": 1462.78759765625,
      "height": 1890,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#121212",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 2,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aE",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 825713000,
      "version": 1295,
      "versionNonce": 416930901,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1776233590119,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. DAU - assume 300M unique users\n2. MAU - assume 1B unique users\n\n\n3. throughput\n    \n    write: in how many way user can write in our system ? \n            just 1 using create endpoint\n            \n            assume 10% of DAU creates url : 30M urls / day = 30m users \n            assume each users create 5 urls / day \n\n            150M shorten url / day\n\n\n    read: in how many way user can read from our system ?\n            just 1 using  shorl url -> long endpoint\n\n            assume each of users are sending req retrive long urls\n            assume each user sends 20 time req per day to retrive\n\n            300m * 20 = 6B read req / day\n\n\n4. storage estimation\n    assume for each user short url + long url + metadata is stored in db\n\n    avg long url  = 100, avg short url = 30, avg metadata = 70\n\n    100 + 30 + 70  = 200 bytes\n    \n    Now we have 150 M / day create short url  (from throughput est)\n\n    so 150 M * 200 byte  =  30 GB / day\n    total storage require for 10 years = 30 GB * 365 * 10 = 120000 GB = 120 TB\n\n\n5. Memory estimation (cache)\n    we need 30gb / day \n     \n    we can store 30gb / day since its small and 1 day expiration\n",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. DAU - assume 300M unique users\n2. MAU - assume 1B unique users\n\n\n3. throughput\n    \n    write: in how many way user can write in our system ? \n            just 1 using create endpoint\n            \n            assume 10% of DAU creates url : 30M urls / day = 30m users \n            assume each users create 5 urls / day \n\n            150M shorten url / day\n\n\n    read: in how many way user can read from our system ?\n            just 1 using  shorl url -> long endpoint\n\n            assume each of users are sending req retrive long urls\n            assume each user sends 20 time req per day to retrive\n\n            300m * 20 = 6B read req / day\n\n\n4. storage estimation\n    assume for each user short url + long url + metadata is stored in db\n\n    avg long url  = 100, avg short url = 30, avg metadata = 70\n\n    100 + 30 + 70  = 200 bytes\n    \n    Now we have 150 M / day create short url  (from throughput est)\n\n    so 150 M * 200 byte  =  30 GB / day\n    total storage require for 10 years = 30 GB * 365 * 10 = 120000 GB = 120 TB\n\n\n5. Memory estimation (cache)\n    we need 30gb / day \n     \n    we can store 30gb / day since its small and 1 day expiration\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "QNfFnFjA3b34N_K7_nqq0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -40444.77083030484,
      "y": -16345.83542346493,
      "width": 1852.343505859375,
      "height": 1890,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#121212",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 2,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aF",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1749036056,
      "version": 2590,
      "versionNonce": 912624053,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1776233590119,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "6. Network bandwidth\n    ingrees: total data entering into system per second (happends when user creates url)\n    \n    we can store 30gb / day\n    so 30 gb enters per day \n\n    30 Gb / (60 * 60 * 24)\n    30 gb / 100k  =  30 mb / 100  =   0.3 mb / sec\n\n\n\n    egress : total data flowing out of system per second (happens when user ask for long url from short)\n\n    we have  6B read req / day (from throughput)\n    each req has 200 byte of data \n\n    total data = 6B  *  200b   =   1200 GB     (billion = 10⁹ = GB in storage)\n\n    1200 GB / 100 K   =  1.2 GB / 100   =   12 MB / sec\n\n\n7. Total servers requires \n   \n    total req / day  =  6B + 150M  =  assume 6.5 B\n\n    request per second (QPS) =   6.5B / 100K \n                            =  6.5 / 100    M \n                            =  6.5 * 10 cube  / 100    K\n                            =  65 K queries / second\n\n\n    assume 1 server = 50 thread \n    and latency is 200ms for 1 req from non funcitonal req \n    1s it process 5 req approximately\n\n    and we have 50 threads  =  250 reqs / second in  1 server\n\n\n    now we have 65k queries / second \n    and in 1 second, 1 server is capable of handling 250 req \n\n    total server  =  65k  /  250   =  75k  / 250     =   300 servers   ",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "6. Network bandwidth\n    ingrees: total data entering into system per second (happends when user creates url)\n    \n    we can store 30gb / day\n    so 30 gb enters per day \n\n    30 Gb / (60 * 60 * 24)\n    30 gb / 100k  =  30 mb / 100  =   0.3 mb / sec\n\n\n\n    egress : total data flowing out of system per second (happens when user ask for long url from short)\n\n    we have  6B read req / day (from throughput)\n    each req has 200 byte of data \n\n    total data = 6B  *  200b   =   1200 GB     (billion = 10⁹ = GB in storage)\n\n    1200 GB / 100 K   =  1.2 GB / 100   =   12 MB / sec\n\n\n7. Total servers requires \n   \n    total req / day  =  6B + 150M  =  assume 6.5 B\n\n    request per second (QPS) =   6.5B / 100K \n                            =  6.5 / 100    M \n                            =  6.5 * 10 cube  / 100    K\n                            =  65 K queries / second\n\n\n    assume 1 server = 50 thread \n    and latency is 200ms for 1 req from non funcitonal req \n    1s it process 5 req approximately\n\n    and we have 50 threads  =  250 reqs / second in  1 server\n\n\n    now we have 65k queries / second \n    and in 1 second, 1 server is capable of handling 250 req \n\n    total server  =  65k  /  250   =  75k  / 250     =   300 servers   ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "g39r4Yo9yCwnoW5iPVVYK",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -42041.78039256917,
      "y": -14017.408103775924,
      "width": 446.4718322753906,
