      "seed": 248071605,
      "version": 488,
      "versionNonce": 1595868460,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1776234149136,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\nindex and pk : shortURL",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\nindex and pk : shortURL",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "wp6bEteutt_e2xV7E3I0o",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -41897.387535426315,
      "y": -1389.0410402838677,
      "width": 2165.3994140625,
      "height": 810,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b8d",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 819629332,
      "version": 704,
      "versionNonce": 1139321388,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1776234150411,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Now once long url is fetched we have to return to user \nwe have 2 options : \n\n301: permanent redirect \n        here its like, browser will store mapping of short and long url so if user req again same then req will not go to server\n        so this will reduce calls to db\n\n302: Temporary Redirect\n        here it always go to server to get long url\n        \n        so if we need to keep track of no of click (analytical data then we shoudl use 302\n\n        else if we want to reduce call to our server then we use 301\n\n        discuss this will interviewer\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Now once long url is fetched we have to return to user \nwe have 2 options : \n\n301: permanent redirect \n        here its like, browser will store mapping of short and long url so if user req again same then req will not go to server\n        so this will reduce calls to db\n\n302: Temporary Redirect\n        here it always go to server to get long url\n        \n        so if we need to keep track of no of click (analytical data then we shoudl use 302\n\n        else if we want to reduce call to our server then we use 301\n\n        discuss this will interviewer\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
